# Trivy: checked findings that are deliberately accepted
#
# The release stops when Trivy finds a vulnerability of the level HIGH or CRITICAL for which a fixed version exists.
# If it cannot be fixed (yet) and demonstrably cannot be exploited in SAMONBOARDING, it is entered here - always with
# the reason in the comment line directly above and an expiry date (at most one year). After the expiry date Trivy
# reports the finding again, so it is checked again. Checked by "python3 scripts/pins.py trivyignore-check".
#
# Example:
#   # libfoo: only used by the print service, which never runs in the container - checked 2026-10-25
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2027-01-31
#
# Empty = nothing is ignored.
